@startuml figure-11-02-upcycling-flow
' Figure 11-2 - The upcycling flow: from an existing Teradata
' transformation to a draft data product in the marketplace.
' The script is referenced, not rewritten.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor black
  BackgroundColor white
}

|Agent|
start
:1. Read the transformation script
(BTEQ / stored procedure);
note right
  Extracts source tables,
  columns used, join logic,
  target table
end note

:2. Reconcile source tables
with existing contracts;

|Marketplace|
if (Contract exists for source table?) then  (no)
  :Flag gap;
  |Agent|
  :Draft minimal source contract
  from DDL (as with DDL / Chapter 2);
else  (yes)
|Marketplace|
  :Reference as input contract;
endif

|Agent|
:3. Draft the output contract (ODCS)
schema, types, inferred descriptions,
proposed tags;
note right
  Proposals, not verdicts:
  a pii tag is suggested,
  never self-approved
end note

:4. Bundle the product (ODPS)
output port + input ports
+ team block awaiting names;

:5. Point the SBOM at the
existing script in source control;
note right  
  The script is referenced,
  not rewritten.
  Lineage by design:
    input contracts 
  + SBOM
  + output contract
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    lineage
end note

:6. Register in the marketplace;

|Marketplace|
:Draft data product visible
status: draft
pre-scored against OMMS;

|Humans (Beth + Cindy)|
:Review tags, name an owner,
set SLAs, verify lineage;
note right
  The agent does not
  have signing pivileges:
  humans (in the loop) 
  own the promise
end note

|Marketplace|
:Promote to active;
stop
@enduml
